    <string name="hub_list_helpBody1">Power actions run immediately without confirmation (same as the computer page).</string>
    <string name="hub_list_helpBody2">Wake: send a magic packet — configure the MAC and enable Wake-on-LAN in the BIOS.</string>
    <string name="hub_list_helpBody3">Sleep: suspend to RAM; the web service stops — the computer shows offline until woken (needs MAC and WoL).</string>
    <string name="hub_list_helpBody4">Shut down: powers off immediately; the web service stops — afterwards only Wake works (needs MAC) or the physical power button.</string>
    <string name="hub_list_helpBody5">Restart: reboots immediately; the web session drops — it comes back online automatically after reboot.</string>
    <string name="hub_list_helpBody6">Without a power route it calls this computer\'s own /api/power (must be reachable); with a route it sends a LAN SOL packet.</string>
    <string name="hub_list_helpBody7">The rEFInd / RefindPlus / GRUB / systemd-boot / OpenCore / Clover choice is written to that computer\'s boot config, effective on next reboot; use Undo to revert.</string>
    <string name="hub_list_helpBody8">The four power buttons are always clickable (same as mobile); boot entries can\'t be changed while offline.</string>
    <string name="hub_list_helpBody9">“Not detected” means that computer doesn\'t have that boot manager installed.</string>
